  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-02T18:29:22.847Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "BCtguZwIvhyM/MZmudFpMJGedqwuial1my+QCsLG7GejCFx65Cc3HDZNClWcIWSnEDPeXhJ5OeYU1e12hTprlA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 240839,
  "published": "2026-08-02T18:26:48.603Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.14: corrections that came out of adopting alpha.13 in a real consumer -- read UPGRADE.md 27. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: IMyIdentityPermissionAdminService.GetRolePermissionsAsync now returns the module catalog's canonical ModuleCode on every row, resolved store-side so the database collation decides the match; rows written before alpha.13 that carry the caller's spelling are normalised on read, and a row whose module is no longer in the catalog is returned untouched. Delete any case-insensitive cross-match you wrote against your module catalog for rows you read through the service: an exact-match lookup is now sufficient and correct there. Each returned entity is a read projection, not a write handle. Added: MyIdentityMessageDescriberAudit.FindUntranslated(Type), which reports the public virtual messages a MyIdentityMessageDescriber subclass has not overridden and which therefore still render in English -- bind it with a one-line assertion in your own test suite. Documentation: the privileged-role comparison rule published in section 25 was wrong for a tenant-owned role named like a built-in, where following it deletes the check, and said nothing about comparisons inside an IQueryable predicate; it is corrected in place. Section 26 now names both legacy-row symptoms (silent revocation under a replace-all write path, zombie grant plus duplicate key under an upsert) and gives the detection query that actually works. API may still change before stable.",
